      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-241803",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/3d/3d3282c834f32ef1d11d8ad263c70b253e21a824dcf647d2a01b119f70eeeb0a.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, the lines $BD^(\u27f7)$ and $FG^(\u27f7)$ are crossed by the transversal $CH^(\u27f7)$ and $\u2220AEF\u2245\u2220DAE$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> *$BD^(\u27f7)$ and $FG^(\u27f7)$ are parallel.*\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $\u2220AEF\u2245\u2220DAE$ | Given |\n| 2 | $\u2220DAE\u2245\u2220CAB$ | {{field-1}} |\n| 3 | {{field-2}} | Transitive property of congruence |\n| 4 | $BD^(\u27f7)\u2225FG^(\u27f7)$ | {{field-3}} |"
