      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-241812",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/e2/e2527bf589309640e42823af0793324fba6d72d388448390ea4ae3e0fb094d04.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, the lines $BD^(\u2194)$ and $FG^(\u2194)$ are crossed by the transversal $CH^(\u2194)$ and $m\u2220CAB = m\u2220GEH$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> *$BD^(\u2194)$ and $FG^(\u2194)$ are parallel lines.*\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $\u2220CAB$ and $\u2220BAE$ are supplementary | Linear pair postulate |\n| 2 | $m\u2220CAB + m\u2220BAE = 180^{\u2218}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| 3 | $\u2220GEH$ and $\u2220FEH$ are supplementary | Linear pair postulate |\n| 4 | $m\u2220GEH + m\u2220FEH = 180^{\u2218}$ | Definition of supplementary angles |\n| 5 | $180^{\u2218} = m\u2220GEH + m\u2220FEH$ | Symmetric property of equality |\n| 6 | $m\u2220CAB + m\u2220BAE = m\u2220GEH + m\u2220FEH$ | {{field-2}} |\n| 7 | $m\u2220CAB = m\u2220GEH$ | Given |\n| 8 | $m\u2220BAE = m\u2220FEH$ | {{field-3}} |\n| 9 | $\u2220BAE\u2245\u2220FEH$ | Definition of congruent angles |\n| 10 | $BD^(\u2194)$ and $FG^(\u2194)$ are parallel lines | Converse corresponding angles postulate |"
    }
